{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["The reason for <b>כְּשָׂכִיר כְּתוֹשָׁב</b> (as a hired worker, as a resident alien): he shall not be with you in your house as a slave but as a hired worker by the year, who is hired for free labor, and they shall not impose upon him heavily. Or <b>כְּתוֹשָׁב</b> — for the way of resident aliens who come to sojourn in the land is that they serve the master of the house with whom they reside of their own free will, as in the matter of Jacob with Laban, who said (Genesis 29:15), \"Are you my brother, that you should serve me for nothing? Tell me, what shall your wages be?\" And in Torat Kohanim (chapter 7, section 3): \"כְּשָׂכִיר\" — just as a hired worker [is subject to] \"you shall give him his wages on his day\" (Deuteronomy 24:15), so too this one — you shall give him his wages on his day. \"כְּתוֹשָׁב\" — just as a resident alien [is subject to] \"you shall not oppress him when it goes well with him\" (ibid. 23:17), so too this one — you shall not oppress him when it goes well with him. \"יִהְיֶה עִמָּךְ\" (he shall be with you) — with you in food, with you in drink, with you in clean clothing, and so forth."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:00:34.412150172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}